From ae0b2ec20f4eb6803d8332962bd429f1f4f824d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:26:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Type a slash /loop tick's submitted prompt row
 loop_tick (TUI + gateway)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A /loop 10m /skill tick submitted the expanded command's prompt as an untyped
role='user' row in the TUI, so once the tick completed kanban_relayed_human read
it as the newest person row (review 5879164478 nit on #1583). Both producers now
type it loop_tick with a language-neutral display_text (↻ /loop /recap):

- TUI _notif_slash_loop_tick and gateway _loop_wakeup_fire_one (via the
  producer-card path; loop_tick joins PRODUCER_NOTICE_DISPLAY_KINDS, so silence
  rules match the internal_notification it replaces).
- The relay's legacy in-flight first-untyped-row skip applies only when no typed
  loop_tick row exists since the fire, so a reply during a typed tick is kept.
- Compressor: loop_tick starts a new turn; Desktop hydration/oracle/types, TUI
  transcript and CLI resume recap render it as its loop line. Not an
  automation-replay kind: the loop owns its own retry.
